{
  "id": "murphy-paranormal-shakti-onsite-amygdala",
  "name": "Paranormal Shakti on-site: amygdala signal, 8-coil cross ('Lady Vampire')",
  "category": "presence",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "fidelity": "approximation",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (Paranormal Shakti software, retired)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "The on-site amygdala session of Murphy's retired Paranormal Shakti, sold to investigators to raise their 'sensitivity' at a site: the amygdala signal alternating between the two stereo channels of a 4-coil cross on each temporal lobe. The vendor links it to the 'Lady Vampire' episode of Paranormal State. The cited pages give no length or switching speed: 30 min and one switch per signal are project choices.",
  "setting": "On site during an investigation (vendor).",
  "schedule": "Vendor: after 6 temporal sessions, do 3 frontal ones (murphy-paranormal-shakti-frontal), but not in the 3 days before an investigation, because it says the frontal session lowers sensitivity. The vendor's general Shakti rules: at most every 72 h or once a week, never on consecutive days.",
  "notes": "The vendor says both on-site sessions 'alternate the signal between the two stereo channels of your computer's sound device' ('Sessions to Use On-Site During Investigations', archived 2013-05-09). The page gives no length and no switching speed. This program runs 30 min and switches after each signal, with about 4 s of silence in between: both are project choices. It is the same exposure as murphy-shakti-60min-bilateral-amygdala-slow at half the length. The coils form a cross on each temporal lobe (FT7, C5, TP7, T9 and FT8, C6, TP8, T10; the site names are this project's reading). One channel drives the top and bottom coils, the other the front and back coils. Each pair has one positive and one negative coil, after the 8 Coil Shakti coil chart: C5, FT7, T10 and TP8 are reversed. The amygdala signal is the project's rising sweep (6 to 30 Hz) with the published point duration and length (230 points of 3 ms, 0.69 s; Ryczko 2002 p.1 [592]). Its point values were never published as numbers, only as a small figure, and the vendor's file is not published. The vendor's 10 to 50 mG carries no distance (measurement.htm, duds.htm); an independent meter read 0.1 to 1.0 uT RMS about 9 cm from the coils (Gendle 2012 p.11 [227]). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. The effect is a vendor claim; experiences during or after a session are not evidence about the site. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). Gillis & Persinger 1993 saw aggression rise with continuous burst-firing (n = 4), not with 1 s every 4 s, the timing closest to this program (Gillis 1993 p.2 [169]). The product is retired; this program is of historical interest. Not for people with epilepsy; stop at once on fear or distress.",
  "targets": [
    "left-amygdala",
    "right-amygdala"
  ],
  "source": "Murphy, Paranormal Shakti: on-site sessions (Wayback, 2013) https://web.archive.org/web/20130509035301/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/Paranormal_Shakti/paranormal_demo/on-site_sessions.htm ; Murphy, Paranormal Shakti: the procedure (Wayback, 2013) https://web.archive.org/web/20130509035643/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/Paranormal_Shakti/paranormal_demo/the_procedure.htm ; Murphy, Paranormal Shakti: frontal lobe session (Wayback, 2013) https://web.archive.org/web/20130509021211/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/Paranormal_Shakti/paranormal_demo/Frontal_lobe_consent.htm ; Murphy, Comments on the Lady Vampire episode of Paranormal State http://www.innerworlds.50megs.com/paranormal_state.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Getting Started (8-coil chart, +/- coil pairs) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/getting_started_basic.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Understanding the 8 Coil Shakti (fast and slow alternation) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_principles.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: What are 'Rapid' and 'High-Speed' signals? (3-ms points, 4-s latency) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm ; Ryczko & Persinger 2002, Percept Mot Skills 95:592 (230-point burst-firing pattern) https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12434855/ ; Healey, Persinger & Koren 1996, Int J Neurosci 87:201 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9003980/ ; Gillis & Persinger 1993, Percept Mot Skills 76:168 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8451123/ ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Safety - how often https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/how_often_is_safe.htm ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 (8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal, sham-controlled) https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/ ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/",
